We will pick up the guests from their hotel and drive to Lepakshi, a historic village in the Anantapur district of Andhra Pradesh. Our first stop is the Veerabhadra Swami Temple, a magnificent 16th-century monument built during the Vijayanagara Empire by Viranna and Virupanna, governors under King Achyuta Deva Raya, brother of Krishna Deva Raya. Dedicated to Lord Veerabhadra, the temple is renowned for its intricate stone carvings, colorful ceiling frescoes, and the famous Hanging Pillar, showcasing remarkable architectural skill
.
